# Root-level .dockerignore - applies to any Docker build whose context is
# the repo root (currently: aws/lambda's Lambda image, built via
# aws/cdk/lib/inference-stack.ts's fromImageAsset). Without this, CDK's
# asset staging hashes/copies the ENTIRE repo - including client/node_modules,
# server/venv, aws/cdk/node_modules (itself), .git, and data/ (which has a
# 400MB+ file in it) - before docker build even runs. That's what made a
# deploy hang for 30+ minutes with no CloudFormation activity at all.

.git/
client/
# data/ is excluded wholesale (raw scrapes, models, html, a 400MB+ file -
# see above) except the three subdirs Dockerfile.render's memory-backend
# build needs (server/app/services/data_store.py) - order matters here,
# each level must be un-ignored before its own contents can be.
data/*
!data/datasets
data/datasets/*
!data/datasets/enriched_descriptions
!data/datasets/cleaned_reviews
!data/datasets/route_geometry
specs/
aws/cdk/
aws/*.md
server/venv/
server/.venv/
server/.env
server/.pytest_cache/
server/tests/
server/README.md
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.md
